  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Immediate Lifesaving Emergency Shelter and Non-food Item (NFI) Assistance for Cyclone and Flood Affected Populations in Central and Northern Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the first and second landfall of Tropical Cyclone Freddy, Mozambique has experienced devasting floods, destruction, and death. Damage assessments are ongoing but early reports from the National Institute of Disaster Management (INGD) show that more than 102,000 houses and homes have been damaged, destroyed, or flooded, leading to the displacement of an estimated 64,418 individuals sheltered in 164 accommodation centers across Niassa, Zambezia, Tete, Manica, Sofala and Inhambane (as of 16 March 2023). Roads and bridges have been swept away, cutting off communities from much-needed support.In response, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing emergency shelter and non-food item (NFI) assistance to 26,7350 individuals (5,350 families) across the affected provinces in coordination with the government and partners, while also strengthening the capacities of other Shelter and NFI partners to respond to the emergency situation. The interventions include strengthening partner coordination and improving their capacity to respond and the construction of 900 temporary emergency shelters in relocation sites for an estimated 4,500 individuals in vulnerable situations.</narrative>
  </description>
